[I] A header-only C++11 library for serialization

[T] cereal is a header-only C++11 library for serialization that takes
[T] arbitrary data types and reversibly turns them into different
[T] representations, such as compact binary encodings, XML or JSON. It has
[T] built in support for most of the standard library.

[U] https://github.com/USCiLab/cereal

[A] Cereal Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[E] opt doxygen

[L] BSD
[V] 1.3.2
[P] X -----5---9 700.000

[D] a3cf744dcb653e64e1a8414422650cbf0e04e996952d63f49bc5d763 cereal-1.3.2.tar.gz https://github.com/USCiLab/cereal/archive/v1.3.2/

